                <pb facs="0514" n="426" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg426"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Baron Komura to Mr. Griscom.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-08-25"><hi rendition="#small-caps">August</hi>
                        25</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Griscom</hi>: The inclosed statement has
                    been telegraphed to-day to Mr. Takahira for communication to your Government
                    There is, however, a prospect of an amicable settlement of the question, as it
                    appears from the latest telegram from Shanghai that the Russian authorities at
                    the port have been instructed to proceed at once to disarm the two war ships in
                    question.</p>
                <p>Yours, very sincerely,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jutaro Komura.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
